District With Bipartisan Track Record", "source": "NewsRadio 560 KPQ", "published": "2026-02-17T08:00:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiYEFVX3lxTFBxeXV1ZjFWcXRhQmJqY0t0ZnoyMklYdU9OSHh1Z1JqeFpuUmxsYU00bUNWaVBfa2dJLUNvWi1KVjVJdk1GVW1reWFJRXBnaU9JUDdsdmN1eVpaN0M0S0NJbw?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": 15.13, "prior_sd": 5.11, "poll_margin": null, "poll_sd": null, "poll_weight": 0.0, "fundamentals": {"margin": 14.99, "lean": 3.0, "environment": 7.9, "incumbency": 2.0, "money": 2.09}, "rating_margin": 15.22, "sigma_race": 7.0, "sigma_total": 7.57, "baseline_margin": 15.13, "analyst_adjustment": -0.13, "key_factors": ["Kim Schrier holds a roughly 20-to-1 fundraising edge, with $3.5 million on hand to Spencer Meline's $89,000", "All nine expert ratings from September put the race in Solid or Safe Democratic territory", "Kalshi and Polymarket each price Schrier's win probability near 97 percent", "Schrier's steady stream of bipartisan legislation reinforces a strong incumbent position on D+3 turf"], "rationale": "Every available signal points the same direction: all nine expert ratings fall in the Solid or Safe Democratic range, both major prediction markets price a near-certain Schrier victory, and her overwhelming money advantage leaves Meline little means to change the race. With no general-election polling, the forecast rests on fundamentals, but incumbency, a Democratic-leaning district, and a favorable environment all align.", "watch": "A late wave of outside spending against Schrier or a sharp national shift toward Republicans in the final weeks would be the main way this race tightens.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Kim Schrier (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Kim Schrier, the Democratic incumbent, enters the general election with every visible advantage in Washington's 8th District. All nine expert ratings published in September place the race in the Solid or Safe Democratic column, and prediction markets on Kalshi and Polymarket each price her chances near 97 percent. She has raised about $3.0 million and holds $3.5 million on hand, while Republican Spencer Meline has raised roughly $127,000 with under $90,000 available — a gap that local coverage has already highlighted.\n\nSchrier has maintained a steady legislative pace, promoting bipartisan bills on the 988 crisis line, veteran mental health, hydropower permitting, and diabetes policy. No public general-election polling exists for this race, so the outlook rests on fundamentals: a district that leans Democratic, a favorable national environment, incumbency, and the money gap. Meline would need a dramatic external shift to become competitive.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9849, "margin": 15.13}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.977, "margin": 15.0}]}